<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Two demon changes that are neither overlap fixes nor cross-mod joins, split out of larger operations.
		  - With ReSplice: Charmweavers installed the succubus drops from poor to terrible with animals. Why the
		    Charmweavers check is there is not obvious; it is the original author's and is kept.
		  - The gatekeeper gains vanilla strong melee damage. This travelled inside an Alpha Genes heat immunity
		    operation, so it only applies when Alpha Genes is installed even though the gene is vanilla Biotech. That
		    gate is preserved rather than quietly widened.
		This folder mirrors Big and Small - Genes &amp; More, which only loads the demon xenotypes under
		RedMattis.Undead or RedMattis.Heaven (see loadFolders.xml).
		Operations that also need another mod sit in a subfolder gated on it in loadFolders.xml.

		Verified against Genes &amp; More 1.6: the succubus does list AptitudePoor_Animals, and the gatekeeper has
		AptitudeStrong_Melee but no MeleeDamage_Strong, so both operations land.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_Succubus"]/genes/li[text()="AptitudePoor_Animals"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<li>AptitudeTerrible_Animals</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
